  "result": "The repository doesn't define an approval limit. Nothing in the code or docs sets a threshold, and UC-2 covers partial approval, not limits.\n\nBased on the conventions in `AGENTS.md`, the rule belongs in `ApprovalService` in `backend/src/InvoiceApp.Domain/ApprovalService.cs`, alongside `Approve` and `Reject`, not in `ApprovalsController`.\n\nFor a refusal, `ApiControllerBase.Handle` (`backend/src/InvoiceApp.Api/Controllers/ApiControllerBase.cs`) maps exceptions to HTTP codes:\n- `InvalidOperationException` → 409 Conflict, which is what `EnsurePending` uses for wrong-state refusals.\n- `ArgumentException` → 400 Bad Request, which is what the missing-reject-reason check uses.\n\nThe repo doesn't say which applies to a limit refusal. Choosing between 409 and 400 is a judgment call.",
